1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,790
In this tutorial, a super administrator
creates a synthetic organization

2
00:00:04,790 --> 00:00:09,100
and enables the services required for the
tutorial tenant.

3
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:12,932
Sign in as Super Admin and open
Organizations.

4
00:00:12,932 --> 00:00:17,242
Before creating anything, search for the
planned Tutorial Demo

5
00:00:17,242 --> 00:00:21,074
name so you do not create a duplicate.

6
00:00:21,074 --> 00:00:25,863
Select Create Organization and enter the
approved synthetic legal name.

7
00:00:25,863 --> 00:00:29,216
Complete the address, phone number, email,
and

8
00:00:29,216 --> 00:00:32,569
tax registration fields with demo data
only.

9
00:00:32,569 --> 00:00:37,837
These values can appear on documents and
communications, so production customer

10
00:00:37,837 --> 00:00:42,627
details must be verified before a real
tenant is saved.

11
00:00:42,627 --> 00:00:46,937
Review the selected status and submit the
form once.

12
00:00:46,937 --> 00:00:50,290
Wait for the success confirmation and open

13
00:00:50,290 --> 00:00:53,164
the new organization from the list.

14
00:00:53,164 --> 00:00:58,911
Confirm that its identifier, legal
details, and active state match the form.

15
00:00:58,911 --> 00:01:04,180
Next, use the organization switcher to
enter the new tenant context.

16
00:01:04,180 --> 00:01:08,490
Verify the organization name in the header
before continuing.

17
00:01:08,490 --> 00:01:13,759
Return to the Super Admin organization
settings and open feature access.

18
00:01:13,759 --> 00:01:16,154
RentAxis keeps optional capabilities
disabled

19
00:01:16,154 --> 00:01:18,548
until they are deliberately assigned.

20
00:01:18,548 --> 00:01:21,422
Listings enables publication and
marketplace discovery.

21
00:01:21,422 --> 00:01:25,254
Meetings enables scheduling between
property teams and renters.

22
00:01:25,254 --> 00:01:28,127
Email Notifications enables supported
outbound delivery.

23
00:01:28,127 --> 00:01:31,959
Lease Renewals enables renewal
opportunities, reminders, and renter

24
00:01:31,959 --> 00:01:32,438
intent.

25
00:01:32,438 --> 00:01:36,749
Gate Pass enables resident visitor
credentials and security operations.

26
00:01:36,749 --> 00:01:40,101
Turn on only the five features required

27
00:01:40,101 --> 00:01:42,975
for this isolated Tutorial Demo tenant.

28
00:01:42,975 --> 00:01:47,765
Save, wait for the confirmation, and
refresh the feature view.

29
00:01:47,765 --> 00:01:52,075
Each selected toggle should remain enabled
after the reload.

30
00:01:52,075 --> 00:01:56,386
Switch into the organization again and
verify that the

31
00:01:56,386 --> 00:02:00,217
corresponding navigation appears for an
authorized tenant administrator.

32
00:02:00,217 --> 00:02:04,049
If a menu is still absent, check both

33
00:02:04,049 --> 00:02:07,881
the feature toggle and the signed-in
user’s role.

34
00:02:07,881 --> 00:02:12,191
Do not enable a capability on a real
customer

35
00:02:12,191 --> 00:02:16,023
tenant simply to make a tutorial screen
visible.

36
00:02:16,023 --> 00:02:18,897
Feature access should match the contracted

37
00:02:18,897 --> 00:02:21,770
plan and the customer’s operational
readiness.

38
00:02:21,770 --> 00:02:27,039
To finish, return to the organization
record and show where legal

39
00:02:27,039 --> 00:02:32,307
details can be corrected and where an
organization can be deactivated.

40
00:02:32,307 --> 00:02:35,181
Do not deactivate the tutorial tenant

41
00:02:35,181 --> 00:02:38,055
while dependent recording fixtures still
exist.

42
00:02:38,055 --> 00:02:41,407
The organization is now ready for users,

43
00:02:41,407 --> 00:02:44,760
portfolio data, and the remaining tutorial
workflows.
